namespace pdg { /**
\class MemBlock
\brief Hold native memory for exchange between PDG APIs.

A MemBlock is either an owned block or a borrowed view of another native object's
storage. Serializer.getDataPtr() returns a borrowed block: keep the serializer
alive and do not modify or clear it while using that block.

getData() and getBytes() return independent Uint8Array copies.
Use those snapshots when the data must outlive its native owner. See getData()
for Node.js Buffer conversion and the copy cost of each conversion form.

\ingroup Serialization
**/ }
